  "description": "The whole outbound path, asserted on the DESTINATION rather than on assets: this integration emits none, so the only evidence it worked is the request that reached the receiver. The export is read with the ET token and the `alive:t` search, and the result is posted to the Sumo HTTP source as newline-delimited JSON, one object per line. The POST-path assertions are the regression test for dst_url. A Sumo HTTP Source Address carries its unique collector code as the LAST PATH SEGMENT (https://<endpoint>.collection.sumologic.com/receiver/v1/http/<code>), so reading it with get_url_base() -- which returns scheme+host only -- discards the credential and posts to the bare host, where Sumo answers 404 and nothing is ever ingested. `requests_absent` on POST / is what catches that; src_url, by contrast, IS a bare console base and get_url_base is correct for it. Export rows carry the real /api/v1.0/export/org/assets.json shape (models.AssetWithJoin): addresses/names/macs are arrays of strings, timestamps are unix ints, and last_agent_id is a nullable UUID, so one row has it null and one has no addresses at all -- both real, and both must be forwarded verbatim rather than filtered or crashed on.",

